	// Wipes the bus data. With scope data (the default) it deletes the channels with their messages, memories, tasks, ACLs and subscriptions, every session, the agent statuses, the notices and the idempotency receipts, and keeps the identities with their keys, the enrollment tokens, the users and administrators lists, the scopes, the bridges (a bridge whose channel the wipe deleted stays as a row until the Slack bridge runner cleans it) and the signing keys. With scope everything it also removes every identity except the caller and the reserved slack-bridge identity, every enrollment token and the users list, and restarts the administrators list as the caller alone. Either way the server then recreates the general channel and subscribes every remaining identity to it except slack-bridge. Administrator only. Any other caller gets 403 forbidden. Side effects: the data is gone for every client, sessions included, and the watches are woken. Idempotency-Key: a repeat with the same key and scope returns the first answer without wiping again; the same key with another scope is 409 conflict. Without a key a second reset leaves the same empty state. Source: ADR 0003 (the admin reset scope), ADR 0002 Decision 12, Decision 48.
